  "description": {
    "raw": "The spell forces the target to believe that nothing in its hoard\nis missing or has been disturbed. This spell fools all the senses,\nconvincing the target that its hoard feels and behaves as it\nshould. Only if the target tries to use an item from this illusory\nhoard for some other purpose does it receive another saving\nthrow to disbelieve the effects of the spell (a wizard trying to\nuse an illusory wand or a dragon trying to unlock a door with\nan illusory key). For the purposes of this spell, a hoard is any\namount of treasure that is too big to be carried by the treasure’s\nowner without magical tools such as bags of holding or portable\nholes, such as a dragon’s hoard, a king’s treasury, a merchant’s\nstrongbox, or a thief’s hidden cache.\n\nThe material component is any item worth 10 gp or more taken\nfrom the original hoard. This item is consumed by the spell.",
    "search_text": "\"the spell forces the target to believe that nothing in its hoard\\nis missing or has been disturbed. this spell fools all the senses,\\nconvincing the target that its hoard feels and behaves as it\\nshould. only if the target tries to use an item from this illusory\\nhoard for some other purpose does it receive another saving\\nthrow to disbelieve the effects of the spell (a wizard trying to\\nuse an illusory wand or a dragon trying to unlock a door with\\nan illusory key). for the purposes of this spell, a hoard is any\\namount of treasure that is too big to be carried by the treasure’s\\nowner without magical tools such as bags of holding or portable\\nholes, such as a dragon’s hoard, a king’s treasury, a merchant’s\\nstrongbox, or a thief’s hidden cache.\\n\\nthe material component is any item worth 10 gp or more taken\\nfrom the original hoard. this item is consumed by the spell.\"",
    "sections": []
  },
